    "formContent": "<div class=\"ielts-form-container\"><div class=\"form-section\"><div class=\"form-title\" style=\"text-align:center;font-weight:700;\">The Africa clawed frog (Xenopus laevis)</div><p><strong>Description</strong></p><ul style=\"line-height:2;\"><li>Skin is <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"31\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"> and can vary in colour</li><li>Skin is coated with a slippery film for <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"32\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"></li><li>Males are <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"33\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"> the size of females</li></ul><p><strong>Habitats</strong></p><ul style=\"line-height:2;\"><li>Native to Africa</li><li>Live in fresh water &ndash; prefered water that is <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"34\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"></li><li>Can survive high levels of <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"35\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"> in water</li><li>Cannot survive if there is any metal in water</li><li>In drought conditions, may live in <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"36\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"> for up to a year</li></ul><p><strong>Diet</strong></p><ul style=\"line-height:2;\"><li>Eat living or dead water creatures</li><li>Find food using their sense of <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"37\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\">, their fingers, and their lateral lines</li><li>Take food into their mouths using from legs and a <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"38\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"> system</li></ul><p><strong>Other information</strong></p><ul style=\"line-height:2;\"><li>Now popular as a pet in the US</li><li>In some US states they are identified as a <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"39\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"></li><li>Used in laboratories for developmental research</li><li>Mucus from the skin was <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"40\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"> properties</li></ul></div></div>",
